- Don’t rely on attribute order: Always parse the 9th column by splitting on ; and matching key=... pairs.
- Handle multiple parents: Parent can be a comma-separated list; split and process each parent.
- Support feature synonyms: Some files use transcript while others use mRNA. Check your file and match both when needed.
- Strip typed prefixes: Ensembl-style IDs often look like gene:..., transcript:..., exon:.... Strip them before comparisons.
- Skip comment/meta lines: Always ignore header/meta lines starting with #.
- Case sensitivity: GFF3 attribute keys (ID, Parent, Name) are case-sensitive.
- Validate assumptions: Quickly inspect rows to confirm feature names and attribute formats:
